description:
**Glassworks London** is an independent women’s fashion retailer founded in 2010, operating across UK retail stores, ecommerce and international production.

**THE ROLE**

We are looking for an exceptionally talented Fashion Creative Director to define and elevate the visual world of Glassworks, with an immediate focus on creating outstanding fashion photography, fashion film and campaign content.

You will bring distinctive fashion taste, strong visual storytelling and proven experience directing fashion shoots and moving-image production. Your work will shape how Glassworks looks and feels across campaigns, ecommerce homepages, advertising, social content and other customer-facing channels.

Working closely with the Founder / CEO, Marketing team and specialist producers, you will develop compelling creative concepts, select and direct talent, establish photographic and film standards, and ensure the resulting work feels recognisably Glassworks.

Beyond imagery, we would love someone capable of helping evolve the broader brand aesthetic across typography, colour, packaging, branded products, retail environments and customer experience. However, excellence in fashion photography and film direction is the essential foundation of this role.

We welcome exceptional senior Fashion Art Directors with the capability and ambition to take on broader creative leadership.

**WORKING PATTERN / LOCATION**

Flexible location and engagement structure, with remote work possible for creative development and direction. The successful candidate must be available for agreed fashion productions and other essential in-person creative work in London or relevant production locations.

Substantial part-time or retained freelance arrangements may be considered according to capability, availability and the scope of responsibility.

**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**

* Fashion photography: Conceive and direct distinctive fashion photography for campaigns, ecommerce model imagery, ecommerce homepages, advertising, launches and other brand communications, establishing clear standards for casting, styling, lighting, composition, mood, image selection, retouching and final creative approval.
* Fashion film and videography: Develop and direct fashion films, campaign videos, motion-led content and other brand moving-image work, including creative concepts, shot direction, movement, pacing, editing approach, colour treatment, music and final creative approval.
* Creative concepts and campaign direction: Translate product, customer and marketing objectives into compelling visual concepts and narratives that build fashion desirability and support commercial performance.
* Fashion taste and brand identity: Develop and protect a distinctive Glassworks aesthetic, building on its London roots, Korean fashion influences, cultural energy, style, personality and existing creative references.
* Casting and styling: Direct the selection of models, stylists, hair and makeup talent, wardrobe, accessories and other elements contributing to the final fashion image or film.
* Creative production leadership: Work with the Creative Producer to select photographers, videographers, stylists and other specialist talent, prepare production briefs, review plans and direct the creative outcome.
* Social visual direction: Establish the creative principles for social imagery and video, including fashion aesthetics, visual storytelling, editing style and music direction, while working with Social Content & Community on platform formats, scripts, programming and audience requirements.
* AI imagery and creative technology: Guide the visual and fashion standards for AI-assisted ecommerce and campaign imagery, working with AI image creators and retouchers to maintain product accuracy, brand consistency, model quality, styling and photographic credibility.
* Brand identity development: Help refine the Glassworks visual identity, including typography, colour palette, graphic language and branded communications, recruiting and directing specialist graphic designers where appropriate.
* Packaging and branded products: Develop creative direction for packaging, tote bags, labels, swing tags, branded accessories and considered brand applications on selected products, in collaboration with Product and Buying.
* Retail and customer experience: Establish relevant creative standards for store atmosphere, music, visual communication, uniforms, packaging presentation and other physical expressions of the brand.
* Creative standards and capability: Build clear, practical visual references and creative rules, develop a strong specialist talent network, review output and enable internal teams to produce consistently on-brand work without continual Founder intervention.
* AI-forward creative practice: Actively explore AI and emerging creative technologies to improve research, concept development, visual experimentation and production efficiency while maintaining original creative judgement, technical accuracy and strong brand standards.

**WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR**

We are looking for evidence of:

* substantial professional experience in fashion creative direction or fashion art direction, with a strong portfolio of personally directed fashion photography and fashion film;
* exceptional taste in fashion styling, models, casting, image composition, lighting, photography and moving-image storytelling;
* demonstrated ability to conceive and direct commercially effective fashion campaigns from concept through final imagery;
* strong understanding of contemporary fashion, youth culture, visual trends and relevant London and Korean fashion influences;
* proven experience briefing and directing photographers, videographers, stylists, hair and makeup teams, editors and specialist creative talent;
* the ability to develop visual concepts that translate across ecommerce, advertising, campaign and social channels;
* sound judgement about budgets and production resources, with the ability to create exceptional work without relying on unnecessarily expensive production;
* a strong creative point of view combined with respect for established brand identity and the ability to recognise what should be preserved;
* confident collaboration with Marketing, Product, Retail and production teams;
* an enthusiastic, discerning approach to AI and emerging creative technology, with appropriate human review and quality control.

Experience shaping typography, colour, packaging, graphic identity, retail atmosphere or broader brand-world development would be particularly valuable.

**WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE**

Strong performance will be visible when:

* Glassworks consistently produces distinctive, desirable fashion photography and film;
* campaigns, ecommerce model imagery, homepage imagery and advertising have a stronger and more recognisable fashion aesthetic;
* casting, styling, lighting, movement, editing, retouching and image selection meet clear creative standards;
* physical photography and AI-assisted ecommerce imagery belong to a coherent visual world;
* production teams can execute compelling fashion content from well-developed briefs;
* Social receives strong visual principles and assets while retaining the speed required for effective channel programming;
* AI-generated imagery reflects the approved brand aesthetic while accurately representing the merchandise;
* the brand's broader visual language becomes sharper, more cohesive and commercially useful;
* packaging, graphic identity and retail creative standards develop where appropriate;
* and the Founder is no longer required to personally establish, art-direct and protect every creative decision.

**Glassworks London** is an independent women’s fashion retailer founded in 2010, operating across UK retail stores, ecommerce and international production.

**THE ROLE**

We are looking for an exceptional Fashion Art Director to elevate the fashion imagery of Glassworks across photography, film, ecommerce and AI-assisted content.

This role is for someone with outstanding fashion taste and a strong portfolio of personally art-directed fashion imagery. You will shape casting, styling, photography, lighting, hair and makeup, composition, movement and final image selection, ensuring Glassworks consistently produces desirable, distinctive and commercially effective fashion content.

Working with the Founder / CEO, Marketing team, Creative Producer and specialist creative contributors, you will translate approved brand and campaign objectives into strong visual concepts and direct their execution from initial treatment through final approved assets.

The immediate priority is fashion photography and fashion image-making. We need someone capable of selecting and directing models, photographers, stylists, hair and makeup artists and other creative talent, and of establishing a consistent photographic standard across physical shoots and AI-generated imagery.

This is not a production-management role. The Creative Producer owns budgets, bookings, logistics, schedules, sample coordination, production administration and asset delivery. The Fashion Art Director owns creative concepts, casting and talent direction, visual standards and final creative approval, working with the Producer to select and secure the right creative team. Exceptional candidates may have the opportunity to grow into broader Creative Direction over time.

**WORKING PATTERN / LOCATION**

Flexible location and engagement structure, with remote work possible for concept development, treatments, reviews and creative direction.

The successful candidate must be available for agreed fashion productions and other essential in-person creative work in London or relevant production locations.

Part-time, retained freelance or project-based arrangements may be considered according to capability and availability.

**KEY RESPONSIBILITIES**

* Fashion photography art direction: Develop and direct distinctive fashion photography for campaigns, ecommerce model imagery, ecommerce homepages, advertising, launches, social content and other customer-facing communications.
* Casting and model direction: Define casting requirements, assess and select suitable models, and direct model performance, pose, expression, attitude and movement to achieve the intended fashion image.
* Styling direction: Direct fashion styling, wardrobe, layering, footwear, accessories and proportions, ensuring styling supports the product, customer, brand identity and commercial objective.
* Photographer and creative-talent selection: Work with the Creative Producer to assess and select photographers, videographers, stylists, hair and makeup artists and other specialist contributors appropriate to each project and the Glassworks aesthetic.
* Photographic standards: Establish clear creative standards for lighting, composition, framing, camera perspective, crop, mood, colour, product visibility, model treatment and overall photographic finish.
* Fashion film and motion: Art-direct fashion films, campaign videos, homepage video and motion-led fashion content, including visual treatment, model movement, shot direction, composition, pacing and overall aesthetic. Work with specialist videographers and editors to achieve the intended result.
* Creative concepts: Translate approved campaign, product, customer and marketing objectives into compelling fashion-image concepts, references, treatments, shot direction and visual narratives.
* AI fashion imagery: Direct the visual and fashion standards for AI-assisted ecommerce and campaign imagery, including model identity, styling, hair and makeup, photographic treatment, proportions, composition and final image quality.
* Social visual direction: Work with Social Content & Community to translate channel requirements into visually strong fashion content while respecting platform-native formats, speed and audience needs.
* Image selection and post-production direction: Lead creative image selects and direct retouching, colour treatment, cropping and other post-production decisions through final creative approval.
* Creative briefs: Prepare or contribute to clear visual treatments, casting direction, styling references, shot lists and creative instructions that enable production teams to execute accurately.
* Fashion talent network: Build strong knowledge of relevant models, photographers, stylists, hair and makeup talent and other fashion creatives, identifying emerging as well as established contributors.
* Creative standards and consistency: Build practical visual references and rules that allow internal teams and external contributors to reproduce the approved Glassworks aesthetic consistently without continual Founder intervention.
* AI-forward creative practice: Use AI and emerging creative tools intelligently for research, concept development, visual experimentation and workflow improvement while maintaining original creative judgement and rigorous quality control.

**WHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR**

**We are looking for evidence of:**

* substantial professional experience in fashion art direction or fashion creative direction;
* a strong portfolio of fashion photography personally art-directed by you;
* exceptional taste in fashion styling, casting, models, photography, lighting, composition and image-making;
* demonstrated ability to direct fashion shoots from concept through final imagery;
* strong capability selecting and directing models, photographers, stylists, hair and makeup artists and other fashion talent;
* confidence directing model pose, expression, movement and attitude on set;
* strong understanding of contemporary fashion, youth culture and relevant visual trends;
* experience translating commercial or campaign objectives into compelling fashion imagery;
* strong understanding of ecommerce, campaign, advertising and social visual requirements;
* ability to achieve distinctive imagery without relying on unnecessarily expensive production;
* strong visual judgement in image selection, retouching, colour, cropping and final creative approval;
* enthusiasm for AI-assisted fashion imagery combined with rigorous judgement around product accuracy, identity, realism and brand quality;
* demonstrated understanding of fashion film, model movement, moving-image composition and visual storytelling, with the ability to direct specialist videographers and editors;
* a portfolio demonstrating substantial, personally art-directed fashion photography, rather than primarily advertising, graphic design, corporate branding or non-fashion campaigns;
* and excellent collaboration with producers, Marketing, Social, Ecommerce and specialist creative contributors.

Experience art-directing fashion film, AI fashion imagery or independent fashion brands would be particularly valuable.

**WHAT SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE**

Strong performance will be visible when:

* Glassworks consistently produces distinctive and desirable fashion photography;
* casting, styling, photography, lighting and model direction feel deliberate and recognisably Glassworks;
* ecommerce model imagery presents products accurately and attractively;
* campaigns, homepages, advertising and social receive stronger fashion assets;
* models, photographers, stylists and other creative talent are selected against a clear creative standard;
* physical and AI-generated imagery belong to the same coherent visual world;
* shoots produce strong usable images rather than requiring continual Founder rescue or creative correction;
* post-production strengthens rather than undermines the original creative intention;
* internal and external teams understand what good Glassworks fashion imagery looks like;
* and the Founder is no longer required to personally art-direct every fashion image.
